<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman Republic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman Republic was the system of government of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from the expulsion of the kings, traditionally dated to 509 BCE, until the rise of Augustus in the late first century BCE. Governed by elected magistrates and the Senate, it expanded across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and the Hellenistic kingdoms. It laid the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and, as accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> note, overcame the Macedonian kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-republic.jpg" alt="Roman Republic" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ifly6 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_republic,_territory_44_BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
